imensional vector space is the characteristic polynomial of the matrix of that endomorphism over any basis (that is, the characteristic polynomial does not depend on the choice of a basis). The characteristic equation, also known as the determinantal equation, is the equation obtained by equating the characteristic polynomial to zero.
In spectral graph theory, the characteristic polynomial of a graph is the characteristic polynomial of its adjacency matrix.

